Privacy and User Policy
Effective Date: July 26, 2026

1. Introduction
This policy outlines how our application handles user privacy and network routing. We believe in total 
transparency and privacy-first design: we do not collect, store, or monitor any of your personal data or messaging activity.

2. Data Collection and Usage
No Personal Data Collected: We do not collect, ask for, or store names, email addresses, phone numbers, contacts, or chat logs.

No Message Tracking: We do not read, intercept, or log any messages, notifications, or app usage data.

Zero Logging: Your network traffic and routing preferences remain completely local to your device.

3. Network Configuration & Cloudflare 1.1.1.1
Proxy and DNS Direction: To enable app functionality, the app adjusts your local device proxy/DNS settings to direct DNS 
resolution and traffic through Cloudflare’s public DNS service (1.1.1.1).

Third-Party Service: Traffic directed to 1.1.1.1 is handled directly by Cloudflare, Inc. according to their public
privacy commitment (which explicitly pledges not to sell user data or log IP addresses permanently).

No Traffic Inspection: We do not route your traffic through any private or intermediate servers owned by us.

4. Data Storage and Retention
App Settings: Any configuration preferences (such as enabling or disabling the app toggle) are stored locally on your device.

No Server Storage: Because we operate no external databases or logging systems for user activity, no remote user 
data exists to retain, backup, or sell.

5. Security
Direct Connection: Traffic routed via Cloudflare’s 1.1.1.1 benefits from standard transport encryption protocol protections.

No Data Monetization: We never sell, share, or monetize any user interactions or network metrics.

6. User Control and Rights
Full Control: You can enable or disable the app’s proxy settings at any time directly within the app interface or
via your Android system settings.

App Removal: Uninstalling the app completely removes all local settings and reverts your network configuration back 
to system defaults.

7. Changes to Policy
We may update this policy periodically to reflect app updates or legal requirements. Any modifications will be updated 
directly within the application or listing.

